      "id": 14,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Queue per replica (waiting)",
      "description": "`vllm:num_requests_waiting` per Pod — the autoscaler's input and the alert's expression. A request that is queued at all has already missed the interactive TTFT budget (docs/SLO.md §4), so the red line at 1 is the SLO, not a heuristic. Per Pod rather than summed: the scaler already reads the sum and answers it with replicas; a queue standing on one Pod after the loop has had time to act is the case the alert exists for. Lights on `kind`.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
